  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity will capitalize on the outcomes of the MONDIACULT 2022 and Organization&apos;s comparative advantage in the region, respond to the special needs of the Caribbean&apos;s most vulnerable citizens and promote the role of culture as a key input to development imperatives, a mediator of development processes and partnerships and as a driver of social development and youth engagement.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity will capitalize on the outcomes of the MONDIACULT 2022 and Organization&apos;s comparative advantage in the region, respond to the special needs of the Caribbean&apos;s most vulnerable citizens and promote the role of culture as a key input to development imperatives, a mediator of development processes and partnerships and as a driver of social development and youth engagement. The activity will also support preparations for the UNESCO World Conference on Cultural Policies - MONDIACULT 2025 to be hosted by the Government of Spain in Barcelona from 29 September to 1 October 2025 as a category II intergovernmental Conference. 

There is a regional trend in the Caribbean to design and implement new policies for culture and development which will be addressed through policy advice and cooperation. Additional strategies in this regard would include policy level support through facilitation and contribution to the discourse on the role of culture in development by bringing together government officials and other stakeholders in order to highlight the importance of culture for development within the Sustainable Development Goals and strengthen cultural platforms in the sub-region.</narrative>
  </description>
